    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d195">

                <pb facs="0310" n="240" sameAs="frus:frus1862/pg240"/>

                <head>Mr. Seward to Lord
                        Lyons.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State,</hi>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1861-12-03"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >December</hi> 3, 1861.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>I refer again to your lordship’s note of the 30th of November for the purpose of
                    saying that the case of the two seamen of the British schooner Louisa Agnes,
                    which was captured on a charge of attempting to run the blockade, seems to stand
                    so nearly on the same footing with that of the two seamen captured on board of
                    the British schooner Revere, which I have disposed of in a previous note of this
                    date, that I pray your lordship to accept my reply in the latter case as
                    expressing the opinions of this government upon the former case also.</p>
                <p>I have the honor to be, with high consideration, your lordship’s obedient
                    servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>WILLIAM H. SEWARD.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Right Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lord Lyons,</hi>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">&amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
